    "teach_8": {
      "id": "teach_8",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Percent statements often become proportions.\n\nIf 30% of A = 45% of B, then\n30A = 45B.\n\nA/B = 45/30 = 3/2, so A:B = 3:2.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_8_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_8_step": {
      "id": "teach_8_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "The useful shortcut is to invert the percentages when converting them to the quantities' ratio.\n\np% of A = q% of B gives A:B = q:p.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_8"
        }
      ]
    },
